    short: "Offer to share sound with the screen: a tab's, or the whole computer's when a whole screen is shared. Chromium browsers only.",
    what: "<code>audio: true</code> in <code>getDisplayMedia()</code> asks for an audio track along with the video. The browser decides what sound it can offer, and the user decides whether to share it; in Chrome that's a checkbox in the picker. The stream can have no audio track even when audio was asked for.",
    how: "Shown as <b>audio</b> among the screen settings. With <code>suppressLocalAudioPlayback</code> on, the bench sends an audio object instead of <code>true</code>. Without an audio track the take has no tap and no sound analysis; turn on <b>mixMic</b> to record your voice instead.",
    best: "Share a tab playing a video to test how a page's own sound records, with no microphone in the way.",
