    what: "<code>systemAudio</code> is a <code>getDisplayMedia()</code> option, <code>include</code> or <code>exclude</code>. It's a hint: the browser may ignore it, and include doesn't guarantee system sound is available.",
    how: "<b>browser's default</b> leaves it out; on sends <code>include</code>, off sends <code>exclude</code>. Chrome's default is include. With exclude, system sound isn't offered alongside a screen, though a tab's or window's sound still can be. Meeting apps use it because the system's sound includes the other people in the call.",
