    short: "Offers this tab first in the picker, as its own This Tab choice. Chromium only.",
    what: "<code>preferCurrentTab: true</code> asks the browser to make the current tab the most prominent choice. It suits apps that mostly share themselves, such as a slide deck shown in a call.",
    how: "The bench sends it only when on. It contradicts <code>selfBrowserSurface</code> off (which hides this tab), and Chrome treats the two as mutually exclusive. Sharing the bench's own tab captures the bench, preview included, which repeats inside itself like a hall of mirrors.",
    best: "Rarely useful on this bench; it's here to check whether the browser honours it.",
