    what: "This is the <code>frameRate</code> constraint in <code>getDisplayMedia()</code>'s video options, shown as <b>frameRate</b> among the screen settings. The spec makes the highest rate on offer the shared surface's own, with lower rates made by dropping frames.",
    how: "The bench sends a plain number, which the browser treats as a target, not a requirement (<code>exact</code> and <code>min</code> aren't allowed for screens). Like every screen constraint, it's applied after the user has chosen what to share. The track table shows the rate the browser settled on.",
